Hmm wait, what about a header like "Bearer\ttok" (tab separator)? HasPrefix passes, SplitN by " " gives len 1 → returns false. Before it would panic too, so returning false is an improvement. RFC says BWS (bad whitespace) can precede the token; a more robust version:

```go
func parseBearer(h string) (string, bool) {
	const scheme = "Bearer"
	if !strings.HasPrefix(h, scheme) {
		return "", false
	}
	token := strings.TrimSpace(h[len(scheme):])
	return token, token != ""
