```

Hmm, this returns false for "Bearer " (empty token) — good. And handles tabs/multiple spaces. This is a nice robust version. Note the original returned ("", true) for "Bearer " — meaning empty token true, then lookup fails anyway; both end in 401. I'll go with the TrimSpace version but keep returning ok=true only when token non-empty. Wait — is that right? If token is empty string, `s.UserByToken("")` — would it match a user with empty token? Users imported might have empty tokens? Let me check store/users.go UserByToken. If a user with empty token exists, "Bearer " would authenticate as them — a security hole. So returning token != "" check is genuinely safer. Let me check users.go quickly.

